WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:00.978
- Dr. Strange,

00:00:00.978 --> 00:00:02.340
Captain America,

00:00:02.340 --> 00:00:03.173
Ironman.

00:00:03.173 --> 00:00:04.510
What do they all have in common?

00:00:04.510 --> 00:00:06.487
MCU characters that I'm about to analyze

00:00:06.487 --> 00:00:07.680
for their medical accuracy.

00:00:07.680 --> 00:00:08.650
Bee-woop.

00:00:09.532 --> 00:00:10.446
- Cast you out.

00:00:10.446 --> 00:00:13.766
(electric exploding sound)

00:00:13.766 --> 00:00:16.599
(time-warp sound)

00:00:17.980 --> 00:00:20.710
- That's clearly a case of cosmononotosis

00:00:20.710 --> 00:00:21.543
where uh,

00:00:21.543 --> 00:00:23.775
the cosmos actually penetrates your skin.

00:00:23.775 --> 00:00:24.704
(chuckling)

00:00:24.704 --> 00:00:27.650
(thudding)

00:00:27.650 --> 00:00:29.420
- I think that was legally your fault.

00:00:29.420 --> 00:00:31.030
- Get the first aid kit.

00:00:31.030 --> 00:00:32.378
Do me a favor and don't be dead.

00:00:32.378 --> 00:00:34.150
(Thor gasping)

00:00:34.150 --> 00:00:36.450
- Does he need CPR,
because I totally know CPR.

00:00:36.450 --> 00:00:38.418
- Thank you for offering
to do chest compressions,

00:00:38.418 --> 00:00:41.465
but a person who is awake
and alert does not need CPR

00:00:41.465 --> 00:00:43.610
'cause their heart is beating.

00:00:43.610 --> 00:00:45.530
Otherwise they would not be functioning.

00:00:45.530 --> 00:00:48.071
- You, what realm is this?

00:00:48.071 --> 00:00:48.904
Alphime?

00:00:48.904 --> 00:00:49.800
Nornhime?

00:00:49.800 --> 00:00:50.759
- New Mexico.

00:00:50.759 --> 00:00:52.840
- You dare threaten me?

00:00:52.840 --> 00:00:54.120
Thor, you so puny...

00:00:54.120 --> 00:00:55.203
(tasering)

00:00:55.203 --> 00:00:57.370
- Oh, that's a taser.

00:00:57.370 --> 00:01:00.410
Everything in your body is
essentially an electric process.

00:01:00.410 --> 00:01:02.367
And when you get zapped with 50,000 volts,

00:01:02.367 --> 00:01:05.580
you essentially lose control
of all of those processes.

00:01:05.580 --> 00:01:07.120
Therefore you collapse.

00:01:07.120 --> 00:01:07.953
- Hi,

00:01:09.330 --> 00:01:10.645
just taking a little blood.

00:01:10.645 --> 00:01:12.447
- How dare you attack the son of Odin?

00:01:12.447 --> 00:01:13.667
- [Doctor] We need some help.

00:01:13.667 --> 00:01:15.077
(grunting)

00:01:15.077 --> 00:01:15.910
(thudding)

00:01:15.910 --> 00:01:18.115
- Oh, I don't want to get hit by Thor.

00:01:18.115 --> 00:01:21.448
(crashing and grunting)

00:01:22.393 --> 00:01:23.226
- See, if I was in there,

00:01:23.226 --> 00:01:24.235
I would be boxing him

00:01:24.235 --> 00:01:25.783
like, ah, ah, ah.

00:01:25.783 --> 00:01:27.145
- Yo, I got you something.

00:01:27.145 --> 00:01:27.978
(beeping)

00:01:27.978 --> 00:01:30.228
(grunting)

00:01:32.622 --> 00:01:34.535
- You're no match for the Mighty...

00:01:34.535 --> 00:01:35.368
(banging)

00:01:35.368 --> 00:01:36.201
(glass squeaking)

00:01:36.201 --> 00:01:37.240
- That looks like they
gave him a short acting

00:01:37.240 --> 00:01:38.640
Benzodiazepine, probably.

00:01:38.640 --> 00:01:40.200
Sometimes when we used to do
promethazine and haloperidol,

00:01:40.200 --> 00:01:43.238
but the Benzo seemed to work
a little faster and better.

00:01:43.238 --> 00:01:44.768
- Ladies and gentlemen.

00:01:44.768 --> 00:01:48.647
Today, we take not another
step towards annihilation,

00:01:48.647 --> 00:01:52.553
but the first step
towards a path to peace.

00:01:55.080 --> 00:01:57.490
We begin with a series of micro injections

00:01:57.490 --> 00:02:00.667
into the subject's major muscle groups.

00:02:00.667 --> 00:02:02.390
The serum infusion,

00:02:02.390 --> 00:02:04.680
will cause immediate cellular change.

00:02:04.680 --> 00:02:06.860
- I mean, the reason we
do all our injections,

00:02:06.860 --> 00:02:08.060
well, not all our injections.

00:02:08.060 --> 00:02:09.392
We do some underneath the skin layer,

00:02:09.392 --> 00:02:11.590
but you will also do
intramuscular injections

00:02:11.590 --> 00:02:13.570
for things that need
to be rapidly absorbed.

00:02:13.570 --> 00:02:15.940
- [Scientist] To stimulate growth,

00:02:15.940 --> 00:02:19.060
the subject will be
saturated with (indistinct).

00:02:19.060 --> 00:02:20.960
- I hope it's clear that this is fantasy.

00:02:20.960 --> 00:02:22.870
There's no thing that you
can inject into muscles

00:02:22.870 --> 00:02:23.900
to just make them explode.

00:02:23.900 --> 00:02:26.120
The only thing that is somewhat
similar to this is synthol,

00:02:26.120 --> 00:02:28.260
which is an oil that I've
talked about in the past

00:02:28.260 --> 00:02:30.210
that some TikToker's use
to make their muscles

00:02:30.210 --> 00:02:31.520
appear really big,

00:02:31.520 --> 00:02:32.950
but they're not functionally big.

00:02:32.950 --> 00:02:34.733
Meaning, they're not
stronger by any means.

00:02:34.733 --> 00:02:38.310
(suspenseful music)

00:02:38.310 --> 00:02:40.240
And that's a huge amount of serum

00:02:40.240 --> 00:02:42.522
to inject into each of his little muscles.

00:02:42.522 --> 00:02:45.593
Like he's gonna be edematous, if anything.

00:02:46.624 --> 00:02:48.776
(pressure releasing)

00:02:48.776 --> 00:02:52.404
(triumphant music)

00:02:52.404 --> 00:02:53.237
(record scratching)

00:02:53.237 --> 00:02:54.457
If you only knew

00:02:54.457 --> 00:02:55.290
(whistling)

00:02:55.290 --> 00:02:56.123
how many times

00:02:56.123 --> 00:02:57.070
(romantic music)

00:02:57.070 --> 00:03:00.510
I looked up this image of
his body, in his workout.

00:03:00.510 --> 00:03:02.370
So I can get his pecs

00:03:02.370 --> 00:03:03.970
because I was obsessed with this look.

00:03:03.970 --> 00:03:05.515
Like, this is my dream body right there.

00:03:05.515 --> 00:03:06.676
God damn you, Chris.

00:03:06.676 --> 00:03:09.370
(triumphant music)

00:03:09.370 --> 00:03:10.946
Even the haircut's fire.

00:03:10.946 --> 00:03:12.515
(missile exploding)

00:03:12.515 --> 00:03:14.070
(missile countdown ticking)

00:03:14.070 --> 00:03:15.155
That's a bomb baby.

00:03:15.155 --> 00:03:16.551
(missile exploding)

00:03:16.551 --> 00:03:18.760
(thudding)

00:03:18.760 --> 00:03:21.573
Damage to his tympanic membrane
is definitely happening

00:03:21.573 --> 00:03:24.170
with explosion so close to you.

00:03:24.170 --> 00:03:25.131
Like, ow,

00:03:25.131 --> 00:03:26.590
(futuristic music)

00:03:26.590 --> 00:03:27.650
Oh and he's bleeding.

00:03:27.650 --> 00:03:28.900
That's not a good area to bleed from,

00:03:28.900 --> 00:03:29.821
because that's where the heart is.

00:03:29.821 --> 00:03:32.238
(screeching)

00:03:34.120 --> 00:03:37.120
(muffled screaming)

00:03:38.500 --> 00:03:40.277
Who's performing surgery
with a patient awake?

00:03:40.277 --> 00:03:41.763
That's just torture.

00:03:43.618 --> 00:03:44.451
(exhaling)

00:03:44.451 --> 00:03:45.284
Did they chloroform him?

00:03:45.284 --> 00:03:46.200
That's so evil.

00:03:46.200 --> 00:03:47.360
And the only reason I say it's evil

00:03:47.360 --> 00:03:48.193
is because like,

00:03:48.193 --> 00:03:50.400
chloroforming someone by
allowing them to inhale it

00:03:50.400 --> 00:03:52.980
by putting a, a, napkin over
it, that's doused in it,

00:03:52.980 --> 00:03:53.870
it's not uniform.

00:03:53.870 --> 00:03:55.090
You don't know how much
dose you're giving,

00:03:55.090 --> 00:03:57.070
you don't know how long they're
gonna be knocked out for.

00:03:57.070 --> 00:03:58.942
My worst fear, waking up
in the middle of a surgery.

00:03:58.942 --> 00:04:00.670
I think that's everyone's worst fear.

00:04:00.670 --> 00:04:02.070
We just don't think about it often.

00:04:02.070 --> 00:04:04.160
(suspenseful music)

00:04:04.160 --> 00:04:06.050
That's an NG tube.

00:04:06.050 --> 00:04:08.400
Not sure why he has an NG tube.

00:04:08.400 --> 00:04:10.600
An NG tube is a nasogastric tube that runs

00:04:10.600 --> 00:04:11.930
from your nose into your stomach

00:04:11.930 --> 00:04:13.860
to either pull fluids out,

00:04:13.860 --> 00:04:16.899
or it's to feed him because
he can't eat on his own.

00:04:16.899 --> 00:04:19.149
(coughing)

00:04:22.049 --> 00:04:24.216
(gasping)

00:04:25.520 --> 00:04:26.590
It does come out like that.

00:04:26.590 --> 00:04:27.423
So that is accurate.

00:04:27.423 --> 00:04:28.960
Just kind of gross watching it.

00:04:30.655 --> 00:04:32.784
(ripping and grunting)

00:04:32.784 --> 00:04:34.476
(ripping)

00:04:34.476 --> 00:04:36.515
(suspenseful music)

00:04:36.515 --> 00:04:39.030
And this is where the
medical accuracy ends,

00:04:39.030 --> 00:04:40.213
fantasy begins.

00:04:41.090 --> 00:04:43.200
- What I did is to save your life.

00:04:43.200 --> 00:04:45.820
I removed all the shrapnel I could.

00:04:45.820 --> 00:04:46.653
But there's a lot left,

00:04:46.653 --> 00:04:48.520
and it's headed into your atrial septum.

00:04:48.520 --> 00:04:50.400
- The atrial septum is essentially

00:04:50.400 --> 00:04:51.740
the separation between the,

00:04:51.740 --> 00:04:54.300
the two top components of the heart.

00:04:54.300 --> 00:04:55.840
Now, if there's shrapnel there,

00:04:55.840 --> 00:04:57.500
if it's not causing a problem,

00:04:57.500 --> 00:04:58.770
I guess you could leave it.

00:04:58.770 --> 00:05:01.130
But I don't understand how
it can enter into the septum

00:05:01.130 --> 00:05:03.259
and not cause severe bleeding in the heart

00:05:03.259 --> 00:05:06.700
between the atria, or at
least out of the atria

00:05:06.700 --> 00:05:08.310
into the pericardial space.

00:05:08.310 --> 00:05:09.170
- What is this?

00:05:09.170 --> 00:05:11.960
- That, is an electromagnet.

00:05:11.960 --> 00:05:13.609
Hooked up to car battery,

00:05:13.609 --> 00:05:16.460
and it's keeping the shrapnel
from entering your heart.

00:05:16.460 --> 00:05:17.390
- Basically what he's saying is,

00:05:17.390 --> 00:05:19.496
he's tryna keep the
piece of metal shrapnel

00:05:19.496 --> 00:05:22.730
inside the actual meat of the organ,

00:05:22.730 --> 00:05:25.208
as opposed to the circulation
part of the organ,

00:05:25.208 --> 00:05:27.338
so it doesn't get shot out
into the general circulation

00:05:27.338 --> 00:05:28.660
and end up doing more damage.

00:05:28.660 --> 00:05:31.190
Like, if it starts going into
the brain, that's lethal.

00:05:31.190 --> 00:05:33.750
- Oh my god, is that the thing
that's keeping you alive?

00:05:33.750 --> 00:05:36.673
- It was, it is now an antique.

00:05:36.673 --> 00:05:38.880
This is what will be keeping me alive

00:05:38.880 --> 00:05:40.020
for the foreseeable future.

00:05:40.020 --> 00:05:41.550
I'm swapping it out for an upgraded unit.

00:05:41.550 --> 00:05:43.340
- I don't know what that
monitor is showing behind.

00:05:43.340 --> 00:05:44.173
(chuckling).

00:05:44.173 --> 00:05:45.220
- Is it safe?

00:05:45.220 --> 00:05:46.250
- Yeah, it should be fun.

00:05:46.250 --> 00:05:47.083
It's like operation,

00:05:47.083 --> 00:05:48.740
you just don't let it
touch the socket wall.

00:05:48.740 --> 00:05:49.750
- What's opera...

00:05:49.750 --> 00:05:50.583
What do you mean operation?

00:05:50.583 --> 00:05:51.640
- It's just a game, nevermind.

00:05:51.640 --> 00:05:52.473
- Great game.

00:05:52.473 --> 00:05:53.662
- Okay, great

00:05:53.662 --> 00:05:55.120
(monitors beeping).

00:05:55.120 --> 00:05:56.019
- Maybe take your ring off first.

00:05:56.019 --> 00:05:57.230
- You know, I, I,

00:05:57.230 --> 00:05:59.027
I don't think that I'm
qualified to do this.

00:05:59.027 --> 00:06:00.660
- Yet you feel qualified to give

00:06:00.660 --> 00:06:02.980
very inaccurate advice on goop.com.

00:06:02.980 --> 00:06:03.861
Very interesting.

00:06:03.861 --> 00:06:05.450
(thudding)

00:06:05.450 --> 00:06:06.283
- What is it?

00:06:06.283 --> 00:06:07.170
- GSW.

00:06:07.170 --> 00:06:08.310
- GSW means gunshot wound.

00:06:08.310 --> 00:06:09.780
I don't know why we say GSW

00:06:09.780 --> 00:06:11.880
when it's actually more
syllables then gunshot wound.

00:06:11.880 --> 00:06:13.260
- It's impinging on the medulla.

00:06:13.260 --> 00:06:14.093
I needed a specialist.

00:06:14.093 --> 00:06:16.200
Nick diagnosed brain death.

00:06:16.200 --> 00:06:18.144
Something about that
doesn't feel right to me.

00:06:18.144 --> 00:06:18.977
- We have to run.

00:06:18.977 --> 00:06:20.270
- A Bullet in the brainstem

00:06:20.270 --> 00:06:22.130
is dangerous for so many reasons.

00:06:22.130 --> 00:06:24.094
Mostly because, the
brainstem controls your

00:06:24.094 --> 00:06:26.020
respiratory rate, your heart rate,

00:06:26.020 --> 00:06:27.580
all these autonomic functions.

00:06:27.580 --> 00:06:29.175
If they're not active,
you can't just think,

00:06:29.175 --> 00:06:31.550
heartbeat, heartbeat, breathe in,

00:06:31.550 --> 00:06:34.017
heartbeat, heartbeat,
breathe in, stomach work.

00:06:34.017 --> 00:06:35.717
If they didn't happen
automatically, you die.

00:06:35.717 --> 00:06:38.000
- We need to get him prepped
for suboccipital craniotomy.

00:06:38.000 --> 00:06:39.650
- Not gonna let you operate on a dead man.

00:06:39.650 --> 00:06:41.168
- What do you see?

00:06:41.168 --> 00:06:42.190
- A bullet.

00:06:42.190 --> 00:06:43.370
- A perfect bullet.

00:06:43.370 --> 00:06:44.203
It's been hardened.

00:06:44.203 --> 00:06:46.180
You harden a bullet by
alloying lead with antimony,

00:06:46.180 --> 00:06:47.013
a toxic metal.

00:06:47.013 --> 00:06:48.171
Now that's (indistinct) directly

00:06:48.171 --> 00:06:49.659
to the cerebral spinal fluid...

00:06:49.659 --> 00:06:52.130
- Rapid onset central
nervous system shutdown.

00:06:52.130 --> 00:06:52.963
- We gotta go.

00:06:52.963 --> 00:06:56.198
- He's basically saying some
kind of metal from the bullet

00:06:56.198 --> 00:06:58.553
is impacting his central nervous system.

00:06:58.553 --> 00:07:00.170
Therefore, he's not really dead.

00:07:00.170 --> 00:07:01.862
He's acting like he's brain dead.

00:07:01.862 --> 00:07:04.100
And he's gonna save his
life by removing the bullet

00:07:04.100 --> 00:07:06.201
by doing a radical procedure.

00:07:06.201 --> 00:07:09.090
Only in a Marvel movie.

00:07:09.090 --> 00:07:10.423
- Cranial nerve's intact.

00:07:12.440 --> 00:07:14.030
- Those look like alligator forceps.

00:07:14.030 --> 00:07:16.630
I love using those to get ear
wax out of patient's ears,

00:07:16.630 --> 00:07:18.860
especially when it's like
hard and you could go in there

00:07:18.860 --> 00:07:19.693
and just, like grab it.

00:07:19.693 --> 00:07:21.672
Hmmm, so satisfying.

00:07:21.672 --> 00:07:24.422
(clock ticking)

00:07:25.820 --> 00:07:27.810
Okay, okay this is really funny.

00:07:27.810 --> 00:07:29.180
This is really, really funny.

00:07:29.180 --> 00:07:30.190
And I'm not a surgeon,

00:07:30.190 --> 00:07:31.156
I've never worn this device,

00:07:31.156 --> 00:07:32.713
but looking at this image,

00:07:32.713 --> 00:07:35.980
the things he's wearing on his
glasses to get a better view,

00:07:35.980 --> 00:07:38.800
are they not covering his field of vision?

00:07:38.800 --> 00:07:42.580
And then the actual lenses
are lower than his eyes.

00:07:42.580 --> 00:07:45.297
Oh my God, he can't see through those.

00:07:45.297 --> 00:07:47.260
(car engine roaring)

00:07:47.260 --> 00:07:48.156
- Can you send me the...

00:07:48.156 --> 00:07:48.989
(notification pinging)

00:07:48.989 --> 00:07:49.822
Got it.

00:07:52.606 --> 00:07:53.439
(cars crashing)

00:07:53.439 --> 00:07:55.600
(tires screeching)

00:07:55.600 --> 00:07:56.599
- Who wants a surgeon that

00:07:56.599 --> 00:07:58.860
is getting pictures of patient records

00:07:58.860 --> 00:08:01.760
on their Lamborghini and
then crashing their car?

00:08:01.760 --> 00:08:03.388
(dramatic music)

00:08:03.388 --> 00:08:06.305
(glass shattering)

00:08:09.280 --> 00:08:12.113
(inhaling deeply)

00:08:13.060 --> 00:08:17.300
- Looks like he has a lot
of fractures in his hands

00:08:17.300 --> 00:08:21.421
requiring some kind of orthopedic device

00:08:21.421 --> 00:08:23.590
with pins and needles.

00:08:23.590 --> 00:08:25.920
I, I've never seen it on
the outside like this.

00:08:25.920 --> 00:08:27.410
This is very exaggerated.

00:08:27.410 --> 00:08:29.850
But remember, the bones in
the hand are quite small.

00:08:29.850 --> 00:08:31.460
The carpals are very small.

00:08:31.460 --> 00:08:35.010
So, putting in pins is not
always a simple process,

00:08:35.010 --> 00:08:37.776
especially the big size
pins that they have there.

00:08:37.776 --> 00:08:40.683
(rain pouring)

00:08:40.683 --> 00:08:43.683
(melancholic music)

00:08:44.890 --> 00:08:46.940
It's gonna take a lot of physical therapy.

00:08:46.940 --> 00:08:48.520
So shout out to physical therapists.

00:08:48.520 --> 00:08:51.020
But also, occupational therapists as well.

00:08:51.020 --> 00:08:52.970
Because when it comes
to rehabbing the hands,

00:08:52.970 --> 00:08:54.790
you gotta think about fine motor control.

00:08:54.790 --> 00:08:56.120
Especially for him as a surgeon.

00:08:56.120 --> 00:08:57.264
- [Doctor] Show me your strength.

00:08:57.264 --> 00:09:00.470
(mystical music)

00:09:00.470 --> 00:09:03.635
- This is him getting that
therapy I was just talking about.

00:09:03.635 --> 00:09:04.610
- [Dr. Strange] This is useless.

00:09:04.610 --> 00:09:06.270
- If the patient is struggling this much,

00:09:06.270 --> 00:09:07.710
we have to decrease the intensity

00:09:07.710 --> 00:09:08.840
of whatever therapy we're doing.

00:09:08.840 --> 00:09:09.673
It's about be,

00:09:09.673 --> 00:09:12.029
allowing them to do it
successfully several times,

00:09:12.029 --> 00:09:14.790
and then increasing that
intensity as time goes on.

00:09:14.790 --> 00:09:17.820
- Have you ever known anyone
with nerve damage this severe,

00:09:17.820 --> 00:09:19.870
to do this and actually recover?

00:09:19.870 --> 00:09:21.530
- One guy, yeah.

00:09:21.530 --> 00:09:22.800
Factory accident.

00:09:22.800 --> 00:09:26.610
Broke his back, paralyzed,
his leg wasted away.

00:09:26.610 --> 00:09:28.360
He came in three times a week.

00:09:28.360 --> 00:09:30.842
A few years later, he walked
past me on the street.

00:09:30.842 --> 00:09:31.675
- Walked?

00:09:31.675 --> 00:09:32.709
- [Other Guy] Ya, walked.

00:09:32.709 --> 00:09:34.110
- Show me his file.

00:09:34.110 --> 00:09:36.330
- It'll me a while to pull
the files from the archive.

